sentences.t:
Tu, ne qua manus se attollere nobis
a tergo possit, custodi et consule longe;
haec ego vasta dabo et lato te limite ducam.”

sentences.l:
You, so that no band can raise itself against us
from behind, keep guard and look out far;
these things I will lay waste, and by a broad path you I will lead.”

sentences.t:
Tris iuxta famulos temere inter tela iacentis
armigerumque Remi premit aurigamque sub ipsis
nanctus equis ferroque secat pendentia colla;

sentences.l:
Three attendants close by, carelessly among the weapons lying,
and the armour-bearer of Remus he overpowers, and the charioteer, under the very
horses having caught him, and with the steel he cuts their drooping necks;

sentences.t:
Silva fuit late dumis atque ilice nigra
horrida, quam densi complerant undique sentes;
rara per occultos lucebat semita calles.

sentences.l:
A wood there was, far and wide with thickets and with ilex black
bristling, which dense had filled on every side briars;
scattered, through hidden tracks, glimmered a path.
